E. Dimension Classification
Table VIII in Appendix B presentsη 3 and dimension
classifications. Ranks 1, 2, 4, and 6 are confirmed qutrit
witnesses: the 300-restart optimization finds configura-
tions withλ max >3, providing a constructive lower
boundη 3 >α. The Wagner graph (Rank 3) and Rank 5
returnλ max = 3.000 across all 300 restarts, consistent
withη 3 =α= 3 (numerically indicated pure two-qubit
witnesses).
We note that the claimη 3(W) =α= 3 is alower-
boundresult: the optimization confirms that the best 3D
representation found attainsλ max =α, but without an
SDP upper-bound verification one cannot rule out a 3D
configuration withλ max >3 that the heuristic failed to
find. For the Wagner graph, the high regularity and well-
studied symmetry (Aut(W) ∼= D4×Z 2, order 16) make
the numerical finding credible, and a formald∗ = 4 proof
remains an open question.
