Finally, theC 7 entry in Table III illustrates that a
larger gap ∆ does not guarantee better noise robustness.
Despite ∆(C 7) = 0.318>∆(KCBS) = 0.236,C 7 re-
quires strictly higher visibility (v ∗ = 0.677>0.585).
The reason is structural: the larger vertex count raises
the mixed-state baselinen/d= 7/3, compressing the gap
between the classical bound and the quantum value and
eroding the advantage faster under noise. The critical
